                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I won this game in a giveaway. Subtitles and menu text isn't displayed correctly on Windows 10 \nhttps://steamuserimages-a.akamaihd.net/ugc/857235404788039622/6D7B9DFEFD4A2304EC8FF8B0EC3831D6660C3D77/?interpolation=lanczos-none&output-format=jpeg&output-quality=95&fit=inside%7C2048%3A1152&composite-to=*,*%7C2048%3A1152&background-color=black\n\nAdditionally, some residual text from the Japanese localization for the Sony Playstation made it in the Windows version\nhttps://steamuserimages-a.akamaihd.net/ugc/857235404788139695/2AD14C55CF2B2C28D5C918606F527D50217EA530/?interpolation=lanczos-none&output-format=jpeg&output-quality=95&fit=inside%7C2048%3A1152&composite-to=*,*%7C2048%3A1152&background-color=black\n\nGameplay is rather basic as you fight waves of varying enemies eager to destroy your castle wall while learning new spells as you proceed in the game. As your magic is stored in rings which can break if you use their powers too much there's a certain amount of strategy necessary. Also, the difficulty of the levels ramps up early on.\n\nKrinkle Krusher isn't a terrible game and the game concept has some merit. I wouldn't pay €10 for a game with this annoying text bug. When it goes on sale 90% off like last October you could give it a try.\n\nI give it a thumbs down because of the bug.",
